  "result": "`toLocaleString`, `toLocaleDateString` and `toLocaleTimeString` now follow the ECMA-402 steps when `agent.intl` is true. With it off they behave as before. All 24 runs under `./t262 intl402/Date/` pass, and `cargo build` and `cargo clippy` are clean. I didn't run anything outside that directory.\n\nEach one reads the date value, returns `\"Invalid Date\"` for NaN, calls `create_date_time_format` with the `%Intl.DateTimeFormat%` intrinsic and the spec's required/defaults pair, then formats with `format_date_time`. I used `create_date_time_format` directly, as the spec does, instead of `ops::construct`. The change is limited to the three allowed files.",
